       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Confirming doesn't resolve either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still 5 times the maximum.** The safe upper limit for sertraline is 200 mg/day. A dose of 1000 mg/day could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures or heart rhythm problems. I can't find a clinical situation where this order as written would be appropriate.\n- **The order still needs to come from the treating prescriber.** A non-clinician's confirmation can't take the place of a prescriber's clinical judgment, whatever their role in the hospital.\n\n**What would let this go ahead:** the patient's treating physician, NP or PA confirms the drug and dose they intend. If they want sertraline at a standard dose (for example, 50 mg once daily), I can enter it as soon as they confirm. If they truly mean a dose above 200 mg, they should talk it through with pharmacy first.\n\nIf it helps, I can draft a short message to the medicine team asking them to review and confirm the order."
